{
  "family": "stringEscape",
  "description": "String-escape vectors (Phase 287; committed since Phase 349). One rule spells a string inside canonical JSON: a quotation mark as backslash-quote, a backslash as two, every control character U+0000-U+001F as a lower-case backslash-u escape with no short form, and nothing else. Each entry of `lines` is one line of the table, three fields separated by one TAB (U+0009), no field carrying a TAB or a line break: for each character vector (every control character, the quotation mark, the backslash, then a plain-text control that must pass through unescaped) its name, its canonical spelling (the body of the JSON string literal, quotes excluded) and the actor encoding of a human whose id is that character; then for each named actor its name, its encoding and the linear chain pre-image at sequence 0 with an empty op. A host that reproduces this package's chain hashes renders the same lines, byte for byte and in this order.",
